    "sentence_translations": [
      "Stone Lions by the Bank Entrance",
      "",
      "In China, we often are able to see two stone lions placed at the entrance of many banks, ..",
      ".. one with its mouth open, one with its mouth shut.",
      "Why is this?",
      "",
      "Generally speaking, of these two lions, one is male, and one is female.",
      "From the perspective of feng shui, the male lion with its mouth open means that it absorbs money from all directions.",
      "The female lion with its mouth closed means that money can only enter the bank, and not leave it.",
      "In this way, the bank will have more and more money. For banks, this is an extremely good metaphorical meaning.",
      "Furthermore, lions look extremely ferocious, ..",
      ".. so placing stone lions by the bank entrance also has the effect of making bad people afraid.",
